==============================================================================
PART A -- the engine agrees with the direct moment, and is charge-graded
==============================================================================
  aZ^2+bW+cW^3: engine == direct for m=1..6:  True
  aZ^2+bZ^3+cW^5 (+2,+3,-5): engine == direct for m=1..6:  True
  aZ+bW+cW^2+d (+1,-1,-2,0): engine == direct for m=1..6:  True

==============================================================================
PART B -- REP THEORY: E[P^m] = L(weight-0 projection), and torus-invariance
==============================================================================
  E[P^m] = L( charge-0 part of P^m ) = projection onto the TRIVIAL rep, then radial L.
  The diagonal torus Z->lam Z, W->lam^-1 W scales charge-k by lam^k and PRESERVES E,
  so E[P_lam^m] = E[P^m] for all lam (P_lam = P with charges scaled).  Check:
  aZ^2+bW+cW^3: E[P_lam^m] == E[P^m] (torus-invariant weight-0 projection):  True
  aZ^2+bZ^3+cW^5 (+2,+3,-5): E[P_lam^m] == E[P^m] (torus-invariant weight-0 projection):  True

==============================================================================
PART C -- ATOMS ARE CHARGE CYCLES: transitive = one-sided, cyclic = intransitive
==============================================================================
  A charge-0 tuple = a CLOSED WALK on Z (steps = charges).  An atom = a PRIMITIVE cycle
  (never returns to 0 in between).  One-sided P: all charges one sign => partial sums
  strictly monotone => NEVER return to 0 => NO cycle => TRANSITIVE, nullcone-harmless.
  Two-sided => cycles exist => the moment ideal is generated by the cycle (atom) forms.

           charges  one-sided?  has cycle (atom)?          reading
         [1, 2, 3]        True              False       transitive
           [1, -1]       False               True     intransitive
        [2, 3, -5]       False               True     intransitive
       [1, -1, -2]       False               True     intransitive
    [1, 2, -3, -4]       False               True     intransitive
         [2, 4, 6]        True              False       transitive
  => one-sided <=> transitive (no cycle) <=> nullcone-harmless;  two-sided <=> a cycle
     exists <=> the atom-covering / disjoint-cycle question -- the OCF shape for the
     charge lattice.  in/transitivity is exactly the pivot between the two.

==============================================================================
PART D -- pushing the atom-covering on multi-charge atoms with the engine
==============================================================================
  For charges {+2,+3,-5}: size-3 atom (+2,+3,-5) gives abc; the renewal must also reach
  the size-8 atom (5x+3, 3x-5) = b^5 c^3.  Check the full moment ideal cuts out one-sided.
     E[P^3] = 720*a*b*c
     E[P^6] = 326592000*a**2*b**2*c**2
     E[P^7] = 76204800*a**5*c**2
     E[P^8] = 73229764608000*b**5*c**3
  V(moment ideal) cap two-sided (a or b nonzero, c nonzero) = empty:  True
  => even with a multi-charge (3-charge) atom, the full ideal (reaching the size-8 atom
     b^5 c^3) cuts out exactly the one-sided locus.  The covering completes across levels.
